nu\nExplore Our College\nMission & Vision\nDepartments\nCenters, Institutes, & Research\nCareer Development\nStudent Success\nFacilities & Locations\nStudent Experience & Special Programs\nExplore Our College\nPrograms & Admission\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nCertificate Programs\nPre-College Summer Program\nHow to Apply & Transfers\nScholarships & Aid\nVisit\nMore in Programs & Admission\nConnect & Contact\nLeadership & Staff\nFaculty Directory\nNews & Events\nAlumni & Giving\nContact Us\nConnect With Us\nREQUEST INFO\nAPPLY\nVISIT\nGIVE\nLet Us Help\nSearch\nSubmit Search\nHome\nPrograms & Admission\nScholarships & Aid\nScholarships & Aid\nIn This Section\nIn This Section\nPrograms & Admission\nUndergraduate Programs\nGraduate Programs\nCertificate Programs\nPre-College Summer Program\nHow to Apply & Transfers\nThe Current Page is Scholarships & Aid\nUndergraduate Scholarships\nGraduate Scholarships\nFellowship Opportunities\nVisit\nWe're excited for you to join our College and are here to help you navigate all of your financial support options. Scholarships, student loans, and federal student aid can help make the investment in your education right for you.\nFinancial Support for Your Education\nThe University's Office of Student Financial Assistance is committed to helping you determine your options and secure a financial path that's right for you.\nUndergraduate Financial Aid\nLearn everything you need to know about scholarships, grants, and other financial aid options available for undergraduate students.\nMore About Undergraduate Financial Aid\nExplore Undergraduate Scholarships\nGraduate Financial Aid\nOur Office of Student Financial Assistance can provide you with information about scholarships, grants, and other financial aid options available for graduate students.\nMore About Graduate Financial Aid\nExplore Graduate Scholarships\nPaid Teaching & Research Assistantships\nGet Started with Your Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA)\nFinancial aid packages and loan programs are calculated based on each student\u2019s need. You must fill out the FAFSA each year to determine how much you will receive in financial aid awards and calculate your family\u2019s estimated contribution. The FAFSA also determines eligibility for student loans and the work study program. For quick reference, our FAFSA school code is 001437. Catholic University does not require or review the CSS Profile.\nDetails About the FAFSA\nCalculate Your Costs\nReview the cost of attendance and find resources to help you plan ahead.\nMore About Tuition & Fees\nFellowship Opportunities\nLearn more about fellowships available to students in the College, which offer an additional opportunity for financial assistance.\nDiscover Your Options\nCollege of Engineering, Physics, and Computing\nPangborn Hall 334\nThe Catholic University of America\n620 Michigan Ave., NE\nWashington, DC 20064\nFacebook (Meta)\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nX (Formerly known as Twitter)\nSupport the College\nMake a gift to Catholic University\nAbout\nDepartments\nHow to Apply\nAccreditation\nContact\nResources & Support\nFor Current Students\nFor Faculty & Staff\nEmployment\nAthletics\nCardinal Shop\nLibraries\nDirectory\nCareers\nFor Media\nCopyright & Trademark\nPrivacy\nConsumer Information\nEn Espa\u00f1ol\nDisability Support\nReport Misconduct\nCompliance\nFacebook\nInstagram\nYouTube\nLinkedIn\n\u00a9 1887-2026\nThe Catholic University of America", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/programs-admission/scholarships-aid#main-content"], ["", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/programs-admission/scholarships-aid"], ["", "https://www.catholic.edu/"], ["Request Info", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/programs-admission/request-information"], ["Apply", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/programs-admission/how-apply-transfers"], ["Visit", "https://engineering.catholic.edu/programs-admission/visit"], ["Give", "https://engineering.catholic.